      <ul class="nb-list"><li>\xB5P Section 1</li><li>The I/O Module Interface: Control, Data, and Status</li><li>Week 7 \xB7 BMI3121 Microprocessor Systems     8</li><li>Signal type Purpose</li><li>Control Directs the device's function: READ, WRITE, report status, or a device-specific action</li><li>Data The actual bits sent to, or received from, the I/O module</li><li>Status Reports the device's state, such as READY / NOT-READY</li><li>A buffer, typically 8 to 16 bits, temporarily holds data as it moves between the I/O module and the external environment, smoothing over the speed and timing</li><li>mismatch from the previous slide.</li></ul>
