      "summary": "5 A\u015Famal\u0131 Boru Hatt\u0131 (IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB), H\u0131zlanma modeli, Yap\u0131sal/Veri/Kontrol tehlikeleri, Veri \u0130letme (Forwarding) ve 2-Bit Dinamik Dallanma Tahmini.",
      "summaryEn": "5-stage pipeline (IF, ID, EX, MEM, WB), ideal speedup formula, structural hazards, data hazards (RAW, WAR, WAW), data forwarding, branch penalty, and 2-bit dynamic branch prediction.",
      "theoryHtml": '\n          <div class="nb-section">\n            <h4 class="nb-title">Klasik 5-A\u015Famal\u0131 Komut Boru Hatt\u0131 (5-Stage Pipeline)</h4>\n            <p>Boru hatt\u0131 mimarisi, komutlar\u0131n icra a\u015Famalar\u0131n\u0131 montaj hatt\u0131 gibi \xFCst \xFCste \xF6rt\xFC\u015Ft\xFCrerek i\u015Flem hacmini (Throughput) katlar:</p>\n            <ul>\n              <li><strong>1. IF (Instruction Fetch):</strong> PC/IP adresinden komut baytlar\u0131 \xE7ekilir ve komut yazmac\u0131na (IR) y\xFCklenir.</li>\n              <li><strong>2. ID (Instruction Decode):</strong> \u0130\u015Flem kodu \xE7\xF6z\xFCl\xFCr, kontrol sinyalleri \xFCretilir ve kaynak yazma\xE7lar okunur.</li>\n              <li><strong>3. EX (Execute):</strong> ALU aritmetik/mant\u0131k i\u015Flemini y\xFCr\xFCt\xFCr veya bellek i\xE7in efektif adresi hesaplar.</li>\n              <li><strong>4. MEM (Memory Access):</strong> Yaln\u0131zca Load ve Store komutlar\u0131nda aktiftir; veri \xF6nbelle\u011Finden okuma/yazma yap\u0131l\u0131r.</li>\n              <li><strong>5. WB (Write-Back):</strong> Hesaplanan sonu\xE7 hedef yazmaca fiziksel olarak geri yaz\u0131l\u0131r.</li>\n            </ul>\n\n            <div class="nb-formula-box">\n              $$S_k = \frac{n cdot k}{k + n - 1} qquad lim_{n 	o infty} S_k = k quad (	ext{5 A\u015Famada \u0130deal Azami H\u0131zlanma: } 5	imes)$$\n            </div>\n\n            <h4 class="nb-title" style="margin-top: 16px;">Boru Hatt\u0131 Tehlikeleri (Pipeline Hazards) ve \xC7\xF6z\xFCm Yollar\u0131</h4>\n            <div class="nb-grid-2">\n              <div class="nb-card">\n                <h5>\u26A0\uFE0F Yap\u0131sal ve Veri Tehlikeleri (RAW / WAR / WAW)</h5>\n                <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Yap\u0131sal Tehlike (Structural):</strong> Ayn\u0131 anda iki a\u015Faman\u0131n ayn\u0131 donan\u0131ma eri\u015Fmek istemesi. <em>\xC7\xF6z\xFCm:</em> Harvard Mimarisi (Ayr\u0131 I-Cache ve D-Cache).</li>\n                  <li><strong>RAW (Read After Write / True Dependency):</strong> Komut hen\xFCz yaz\u0131lmam\u0131\u015F sonucu okumak ister. <em>\xC7\xF6z\xFCm:</em> Veri \u0130letme (Data Forwarding / Bypassing).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Load-Use Gecikmesi:</strong> Bellekten veri okuma MEM a\u015Famas\u0131nda bitti\u011Finden, iletmeye ra\u011Fmen 1 \xE7evrimlik duraklatma (Bubble) ka\xE7\u0131n\u0131lmazd\u0131r.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n              <div class="nb-card">\n                <h5>\u{1F500} Kontrol Tehlikeleri ve Dallanma Tahmini</h5>\n                <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Dallanma Cezas\u0131 (Branch Penalty):</strong> S\u0131\xE7rama karar\u0131 verilene kadar getirilen komutlar iptal edilir (Pipeline Flush).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Statik BTFN:</strong> Geriye s\u0131\xE7ra (d\xF6ng\xFC), ileriye s\u0131\xE7rama (hata blo\u011Fu).</li>\n                  <li><strong>2-Bit Doygunluk Say\u0131c\u0131s\u0131:</strong> 11 (G\xFC\xE7l\xFC Al\u0131r), 10 (Zay\u0131f Al\u0131r), 01 (Zay\u0131f Almaz), 00 (G\xFC\xE7l\xFC Almaz).</li>\n                  <li><strong>BTB (Branch Target Buffer):</strong> S\u0131\xE7rama hedef adresini \xF6nbellekte saklar (0-\xE7evrim gecikme).</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n\n            <h4 class="nb-title" style="margin-top: 16px;">Boru Hatt\u0131 Ba\u011F\u0131ms\u0131z \u0130\u015Flemler \xD6rne\u011Fi</h4>\n            <div class="nb-code-box">\n              <pre><code>; Ba\u011F\u0131ms\u0131z \u0130\u015Flemler: RAW Veri Tehlikesi ve Stall Yaratmaz\nORG 100h\n    MOV AX, 10\n    MOV BX, 20\n    ADD AX, 5           ; AX \xFCzerinde i\u015Flem (ALU 1)\n    SUB BX, 2           ; BX \xFCzerinde ba\u011F\u0131ms\u0131z i\u015Flem (ALU 2) - Tam h\u0131zda paralel akar!\n    HLT</code></pre>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ',
      "theoryHtmlEn": '\n          <div class="nb-callout info">\n            <strong>\u{1F1EC}\u{1F1E7} Official Course Lecture Slide Text (Verbatim Professor Content)</strong><br>\n            <em>BMI3121 (Ge\xE7en Y\u0131l / Previous Year) \u2014 w13a.pdf: Instruction Pipelining (Slides 2\u201318)</em>\n          </div>\n          <div class="nb-section">\n            <h4 class="nb-title">1. The 5-Stage Instruction Pipeline</h4>\n            <p>\n              Instruction pipelining is a technique used in modern microprocessors to increase instruction throughput by overlapping the execution of multiple instructions:\n            </p>\n            <ol>\n              <li><strong>Fetch (IF):</strong> Retrieve instruction from memory using Program Counter (PC/IP).</li>\n              <li><strong>Decode (ID):</strong> Translate opcode into control signals and read source registers.</li>\n              <li><strong>Execute (EX):</strong> Perform ALU operations or calculate effective addresses.</li>\n              <li><strong>Memory Access (MEM):</strong> Access data memory for Load/Store operations.</li>\n              <li><strong>Write-Back (WB):</strong> Write the computed result back into destination register file.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <div class="nb-formula-box">\n              $$	ext{Speedup } S_k = \frac{n cdot k}{k + n - 1} 	o k quad (	ext{For a 5-stage pipeline, ideal speedup approaches } 5	imes)$$\n            </div>\n          </div>\n          <div class="nb-section">\n            <h4 class="nb-title">2. Pipeline Hazards and Mitigation Strategies</h4>\n            <div class="nb-grid-2">\n              <div class="nb-card">\n                <h5>Structural and Data Hazards</h5>\n                <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Structural Hazard:</strong> Resource conflict when hardware cannot support multiple concurrent stages (e.g. single-port memory). Resolved by separate instruction and data caches (Harvard architecture).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Data Hazard (RAW - Read After Write):</strong> Instruction depends on the result of an earlier uncompleted instruction. Mitigated by <em>Data Forwarding (Bypassing)</em> from EX/MEM stages directly to ALU.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n              <div class="nb-card">\n                <h5>Control Hazards and Branch Prediction</h5>\n                <ul>\n                  <li><strong>Branch Penalty:</strong> Conditional jumps discard incorrectly fetched instructions upon misprediction, stalling the pipeline (pipeline flush).</li>\n                  <li><strong>Dynamic Branch Prediction:</strong> 2-bit saturating counters (Strongly Taken, Weakly Taken, Weakly Not Taken, Strongly Not Taken) achieve >90% branch accuracy.</li>\n                </ul>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        ',
